    "user_request_original": "Design a planar multilayer dielectric filter with air incidence at 0 degrees, unpolarized illumination, on fused silica substrate. Use exactly 36 film layers in alternating sequence: Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Gao), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Gao), repeating 18 times (starting with Ta2O5 (Gao) adjacent to air, ending with SiO2 (Gao) adjacent to substrate). Optimize all 36 individual layer thicknesses with bounds 15-355 nm. Target bands: minimize average transmittance at 355-365 nm, minimize average transmittance at 1030-1080 nm, minimize transmittance at 355 nm, maximize average transmittance at 420-700 nm. Simulation wavelength grid must span 350-1100 nm to ensure all target bands overlap the grid. Materials: Ta2O5 (Gao) (high index) and SiO2 (Gao) (low index). Substrate: fused silica. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates.",
